{"page_id": "synth_copies-images_sv304cf93e-p1", "markdown": "# Day 4: Financial Statement Analysis and Transaction Analysis\n\nFinancial Statement Analysis\n\nProfitability\n\nEarnings Per Share =\n\nNet Income - Preferred Dividends\n\nWeighted-Average Common Shares\n\nOutstanding\n\nLiquidity\n\nCurrent Ratio =\n\nCurrent Assets\n\nCurrent\n\nLiabilities\n\nWorking Capital = Current Assets - Current Liabilities\n\nSolvency\n\nDebt to Assets Ratio =\n\nTotal\n\nLiabilities\n\nTotal Assets\n\nThe chief financial officer (CFO) of Myeneke Corporation requested that the accounting department preliminary balance sheet on December 30, 2017, so that the CFO could get an idea of how the company stood. He\n\nknows that certain debt agreements with its creditors require the company to maintain a current ratio of at least\n\n2:1. The preliminary balance sheet is as follows.\n\nMYENEKE CORP.\n\nBalance Sheet\n\nDecember 30, 2017\n\n<table>\n<tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td colspan=\"2\">Current assets</td><td></td><td>Current liabilities</td><td colspan=\"2\"></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Cash</td><td>$25,000</td><td></td><td>Accounts payable</td><td>$ 20,000</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Accounts receivable</td><td>30,000</td><td></td><td>Salaries and wages payable</td><td>10,000</td><td>$ 30,000</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Prepaid insurance</td><td>5,000</td><td>$ 60,000</td><td>Long-term liabilities</td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</table>", "width": 1700, "height": 2200, "blocks": [{"kind": "heading", "text": "Day 4: Financial Statement Analysis and Transaction Analysis", "bbox": {"x": 197.03504019958194, "y": 215.41666665722542, "width": 1255.5256064690027, "height": 50.41666666666649}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Financial Statement Analysis", "bbox": {"x": 196.5981404391942, "y": 295.7088214447412, "width": 486.60407464780576, "height": 48.923919598261435}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Profitability", "bbox": {"x": 196.04458725293856, "y": 341.3215576483017